# Trivy vulnerability / rule ignore file (read from the repo root by the scans in
# .github/workflows/security.yml, which fail the job on fixed HIGH/CRITICAL
# findings).
#
# Add a CVE ID or Trivy rule ID per line ONLY for a finding that is understood
# and accepted, and always give it an expiry date and a reason so it is
# re-examined instead of living here forever:
#
#   CVE-2099-00000 exp:2027-03-31   # reason: not reachable (feature X unused); fix pending upstream
#
# File-path exclusions are not made here but via `skip-files` in security.yml
# (currently: the kustomize strategic-merge patch k8s/openbao/patch-server-env.yaml,
# which Trivy would evaluate as an incomplete Deployment, and the CHANGE_ME
# secrets.yaml.example templates).
